GameTheory -- a package for computing equilibria in game theory
***************************************************************

Description
===========

Game Theory is a package for several equilibrium concepts in game theory. It
constructs the algebro-geometric and combinatorial models for Nash, correlated,
dependency, and conditional independence equilibria. The latter three notions
of equilibria are all generalizations of Nash equilibria. An $n$-player game in
normal form is defined by $n$-tensors of format $d_1 \times d_2 \times \cdots
\times d_n$, where $d_i$ is the number of pure strategies of player $i$. The
entry $\{j_1, j_2, \cdots, j_n\}$ of the $i$-th (payoff) tensor for player $i$
is the payoff when player $1$ chooses strategy $j_1$, player $2$ chooses
strategy $j_2$, and so on. One can define a specific game or a random game,
e.g., a list with random tensors.

