The notion of Nash equilibria is one of the central topics in game theory.
*note nashEquilibriumIdeal: nashEquilibriumIdeal_lpRing_cmList_rp, computes a
square system of $d_1 + \cdots + d_n$ polynomials that algebraically model the
set of totally mixed Nash equilibria. In the case where the dimension of this
ideal is zero (commonly referred to as a generic game), one can use the mixed
volume of the Newton polytopes of each polynomial in the system to obtain an
upper bound on the number of totally mixed Nash equilibria. The list of these
Newton polytopes is provided by *note deltaList: deltaList_lpList_rp,. The
mixed volume of these polytopes equals the number of certain block
derangements. The method *note numberTMNE: numberTMNE_lpList_rp, is typically
faster than *note mixedVolume: (Polyhedra)mixedVolume, in this case.

