The set of correlated equilibria of a game forms a convex polytope inside the
(probability) simplex which is the standard simplex of dimension $d_1 \cdots
d_n -1$. Thus, the variables are taken from *note probabilityRing:
probabilityRing,. In particular, the map from *note nashEquilibriumRing:
nashEquilibriumRing_lpList_rp, to *note probabilityRing: probabilityRing, is
the Segre embedding.

