Caveat
======

GameTheory uses Polyhedra.m2 for the methods of correlated equilibria and
GraphicalModels.m2 for the methods of conditional independence equilibria.
Throughout the package, we followed Macaulay2's convention of zero-based
indexing. This can be seen e.g., in the methods of *note nashEquilibriumRing:
nashEquilibriumRing_lpList_rp, and *note probabilityRing: probabilityRing,. In
particular, for an $n$-player game, the players are labeled $0, \ldots, n-1$,
and if player $i$ has $d_i$ pure strategies, they are labeled $0, \ldots,
d_i-1$.

