assemblePolynomial -- compute incentive constraint polynomial for deviation
***************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        assemblePolynomial(PR, Xi, {i,k,l})
  * Inputs:
      * PR, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, Polynomial ring of strategy
        probabilities.
      * Xi, an instance of the type *note Tensor: Tensor,, Tensor of strategy
        probabilities.
      * {i, k, l}, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, A triple where: - $i$ is
        the player index, - $k$ is the current strategy, - $l$ is the deviating
        strategy.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, A polynomial
        representing the incentive constraint for player $i$ deviating from $k$
        to $l$.

Description
===========

This function computes a linear inequality encoding the condition for a
correlated equilibrium: the expected utility from playing $k$ should be no less
than from playing $l$.

+------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[p_{0,0}, p_{0,1}, p_{1,0}, p_{1,1}];|
+------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : Xi = randomTensor(QQ, {2,2});              |
+------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : assemblePolynomial(R, Xi, {0,0,1})         |
|                                                |
|     15          1                              |
|o3 = --p       + -p                             |
|      4 {0, 0}   2 {0, 1}                       |
|                                                |
|o3 : R                                          |
+------------------------------------------------+

