konstanzMatrix -- construct the Konstanz matrix of a given game
***************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        konstanzMatrix(PR, X)
  * Inputs:
      * PR, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, a probability ring obtained via
        probabilityRing(Di), where $Di = \{d_1 , \cdots , d_n\}$ is the format
        of the game
      * X, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of n tensors of format
        $D_i$ describing the payoffs of the game
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * KonstanzVariableName (missing documentation) => ..., default value "k",
  * Outputs:
      * a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, the $(d_1 + \ldots + d_n) \times
        (d-1 \cdots d_n)$-dimensional Konstanz matrix

Description
===========

It is crucial that the formats in PR and X match up. The Konstanz matrix
$K_X(k)$ is the unique matrix with monic polynomials as entries such that the
Spohn variety is the union $\bigcup_{k \in (\mathbb P^1)^n} \ker K_X(k)$.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : Di = {2,2,3};                                                           |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : PR = probabilityRing(Di);                                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : X = randomGame(Di);                                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : K = konstanzMatrix(PR,X)                                                |
|                                                                             |
|o4 = | k_0-9/2 k_0-9/4 k_0-3/4  k_0-7/4 k_0-7/9 k_0-7/10 0        0          |
|     | 0       0       0        0       0       0        k_0-7/10 k_0-7/3    |
|     | k_1-5/4 k_1-2/9 k_1-3/10 0       0       0        k_1-10   k_1-3/2    |
|     | 0       0       0        k_1-3/7 k_1-5   k_1-10/9 0        0          |
|     | k_2-5/3 0       0        k_2-6/5 0       0        k_2-5/3  0          |
|     | 0       k_2-7/2 0        0       k_2-5/7 0        0        k_2-1/10   |
|     | 0       0       k_2-2/5  0       0       k_2-5/9  0        0          |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|     0       0       0        0       |                                      |
|     k_0-7   k_0-3/7 k_0-6/7  k_0-6   |                                      |
|     k_1-7/8 0       0        0       |                                      |
|     0       k_1-5/6 k_1-5    k_1-2/5 |                                      |
|     0       k_2-3/7 0        0       |                                      |
|     0       0       k_2-9/10 0       |                                      |
|     k_2-4/3 0       0        k_2-4/7 |                                      |
|                                                                             |
|                        7                 12                                 |
|o4 : Matrix (PR[k ..k ])  <-- (PR[k ..k ])                                   |
|                 0   2             0   2                                     |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

The optional argument KonstanzVariableName allows to change the name of the
variables. If no variable name choice is specified, the variables will be named
with k.

+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : Di = {2,2};                                          |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : PR = probabilityRing(Di);                            |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i7 : X = randomGame(Di);                                  |
+----------------------------------------------------------+
|i8 : K = konstanzMatrix(PR,X, KonstanzVariableName => "z")|
|                                                          |
|o8 = | z_0-5/9 z_0-5/9 0       0       |                  |
|     | 0       0       z_0-6/7 z_0-6   |                  |
|     | z_1-5/4 0       z_1-8/5 0       |                  |
|     | 0       z_1-2/9 0       z_1-9/4 |                  |
|                                                          |
|                        4                 4               |
|o8 : Matrix (PR[z ..z ])  <-- (PR[z ..z ])                |
|                 0   1             0   1                  |
+----------------------------------------------------------+

