Tensor -- a mutable hash table representing a tensor
****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        T = zeroTensor(R, d)
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note Tensor: Tensor,, A Tensor object storing
        values at multi-indices.

Description
===========

The type Tensor is a mutable hash table with additional metadata to represent
multi-dimensional arrays. Each tensor has an associated format (list of
dimensions), a coefficient ring, and a set of index keys.



+-------------------------------------+
|i1 : T = zeroTensor(QQ, {2,2});      |
+-------------------------------------+
|i2 : T#{0,0} = 1;                    |
+-------------------------------------+
|i3 : T#{1,1} = 5;                    |
+-------------------------------------+
|i4 : format T                        |
|                                     |
|o4 = {2, 2}                          |
|                                     |
|o4 : List                            |
+-------------------------------------+
|i5 : coefficientRing T               |
|                                     |
|o5 = QQ                              |
|                                     |
|o5 : Ring                            |
+-------------------------------------+
|i6 : indexset T                      |
|                                     |
|o6 = {{0, 0}, {0, 1}, {1, 0}, {1, 1}}|
|                                     |
|o6 : List                            |
+-------------------------------------+

